{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527591656,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NTA3OTQ1MDM="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527595726,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5Mjc1MzA1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2581#issuecomment-392753057"},"message":"It's just a `json.dumps` call with a dictionary, same as it has been since run was first added.  It seems weird to label this as a bug, since it's never specified that these fields will be in some particular order within a message or the same order across messages. But I agree that it'd be better to sort the keys so that there's a consistent order when inspecting the logs and so that someone overriding dates will get the exact same commit when running identical commands.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527595779,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NTA5MTg3Mzk="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527595779,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTY1MDkxODc0Mw=="},"added":[],"removed":["severity-normal"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527595788,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5Mjc1MzI4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2581#issuecomment-392753283"},"message":"@kyleam you are right, this is not a bug","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527595805,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTY1MDkxOTYyMg=="},"title":"Make order of keys in `run` record deterministic","was":"Make order of keys in `run` record deterministic"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527600841,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5Mjc3ODM1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2581#issuecomment-392778353"},"message":"\u003e @kyleam you are right, this is not a bug\n\nNever mind, I was wrong!  It was the intention to sort the info keys, since from early on there has been  a `sort_keys=True` there,  but `run` has never actually sorted them because `sort_keys=True` has always been dropped as part of the `format` call due to a misplaced ')'.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527600849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NTExMDM1MTU="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527600849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTY1MTEwMzUyMQ=="},"added":[],"removed":["enhancement"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527606277,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjgxMDkyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2581#issuecomment-392810920"},"message":"one note -- json.dump with indent breeds trailing spaces, while at it you might want to add `separators=(',', ': ')`\n```\n$\u003e python -c 'import json; print(json.dumps({1:2, 3:4}, indent=1));' | sed -e 's, $,-,g'\n{\n \"1\": 2,-\n \"3\": 4\n}\n$\u003e python -c \"import json; print(json.dumps({1:2, 3:4}, indent=1, separators=(',', ': ')));\" | sed -e 's, $,-,g' \n{\n \"1\": 2,\n \"3\": 4\n}\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527608337,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjgyNDAyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2581#issuecomment-392824020"},"message":"\u003e one note -- json.dump with indent breeds trailing spaces, while at it you might want to add separators=(',', ': ')\n\nThanks, I wasn't aware of that.  Git cleans them up for us though (with the default value of commit.cleanup):\n\n```bash\n% printf 'subj\\n\\n' \u003e message\n% python -c 'import json; print(json.dumps({1:2, 3:4}, indent=1));' \u003e\u003e message\n% cat message | sed 's/ $/-/g'\nsubj\n\n{\n \"1\": 2,-\n \"3\": 4\n}\n% git commit --allow-empty -F message\n[master 1c46a2f] subj\n% git cat-file commit HEAD | sed 's/ $/-/g'\ntree 32b97a7332f485ca3b3fd33067b39c1ccd422ae2\nparent 24c75a77c51a4a33cc7e3357c6647508df371ae8\nauthor Kyle Meyer \u003ckyle@kyleam.com\u003e 1527608241 -0400\ncommitter Kyle Meyer \u003ckyle@kyleam.com\u003e 1527608241 -0400\n\nsubj\n\n{\n \"1\": 2,\n \"3\": 4\n}\n```","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527683184,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY1MzQwOTUzMA=="},"status":2}]}